; getline_index_out_of_range: a linear read at the declared extent must raise.
;
; xqvm_py's get_linear was `self.linear.get(i, 0)` with no range check, so
; this program halted there with 0 on the stack while the Rust VM raised
; IndexOutOfBounds: a fault-versus-success divergence on four instructions,
; and the one case no vector reached.
;
; The index is exactly `size`, not a large number, so this pins the off-by-one
; and not merely the rejection of something obviously wrong. Reading index 3
; of the same model returns 0 and is correct, which is the distinction the
; bound has to make: an absent in-range coefficient and a read past the end
; are different outcomes rather than the same 0.

PUSH 4
BQMX r0

PUSH 4           ; index == size
GETLINE r0
HALT
